 file contains no bearer token.","Windows sessions require the matching packaged Windows x64 native addon, local NTFS/ReFS targets and runtimes, and Windows 10 or later. Native handles enforce path admission, private DACLs, and Job Object ownership automatically.","The Ghidra Program references PDB CrackMe.pdb (GUID 224e9bc9-27a5-4ee7-a9f4-5fc49f3f536a, age (hex) 12, signature unknown, version RSDS); Ghidra reports load state unknown. Original names and types may be missing; an empty name search does not prove a procedure is absent. Use list_procedures and address-based analysis to inspect recovered functions. REA does not admit a caller-selected PDB companion.","Known provider defect ghidra-9996 (jump-table-flow-references-omitted): Ghidra 12.2 can omit jump-table flow references and emit incorrect decompiler output for clang -O0 x86-64 switches whose case labels start above zero. Upstream issue https://github.com/NationalSecurityAgency/ghidra/issues/9996 is closed by c93917a622211349998f641de54cfdbe0e0e5bee, milestone 12.2.1, which is not yet released. This limitation is recorded for parsed 12.2 releases whose patch is below 12.2.1, including a zero patch and a suffix, and clears on 12.2.1. REA's verified switch lane compiles with -O2 and does not cover this shape.","Known provider defect ghidra-10154 (jump-table-unrecovered-function-truncated): Ghidra 12.2 leaves an aarch64 switch unrecovered when it is a byte-offset bounded by and-0xff. The function body stops at the indirect branch. Upstream issue https://github.com/NationalSecurityAgency/ghidra/issues/10154 is open and names a Swift -O swift-enum switch; it has no fix commit and no milestone. REA reproduced the unrecovered jump table on the exact 12.2 build with an AArch64 ELF object of that instruction shape. A compare-bounded byte table still recovers. This record stays on every admitted build until a release is known to clear it."],"relationship_coverage":{"status":"complete","diagnostics":["Only resolved Ghidra call references are returned; unresolved computed or indirect calls remain unknown, while function classifications distinguish thunks and externals."],"discovery":{"callers":{"status":"unknown","reason":"Recorded incoming references do not establish additional computed callers elsewhere in the program."}}},"locations":[],"evidence_links":[]}
